@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+---
+id: dl-004-preserve-json-validation-and-immutability-for-merge-patch
+type: decision-log
+title: "Preserve JSON validation and immutability for Merge Patch"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Existing public JSON utilities reject non-JSON JavaScript values and return independent results. JSON
+Merge Patch needs to follow the same library contract while applying RFC 7386's recursive semantics.
+
+## Decision
+
+Validate both merge-patch inputs as JSON values before evaluation. Build the result from clones rather
+than mutating either input; recursively merge only plain JSON objects, and replace the target for every
+other patch value.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Callers receive a valid, independent JSON value and invalid JavaScript values fail consistently with
+the rest of the library. Arrays are replaced atomically, as RFC 7386 specifies.
